        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "ci(swift): enforce shared OpenClawKit dead-code coverage",
        "body": "Closes #105749\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a CI blind spot where neither the iOS nor macOS Periphery lane could soundly classify dead declarations in shared OpenClawKit: each single-platform build reports APIs used only by the other consumer.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe new workflow scans the shared sources from both native consumers in parallel, uploads both raw reports, and fails only on their exact Swift-USR intersection. It retains the generated `OpenClawProtocol/GatewayModels.swift` contract, rejects malformed or failed producer reports, and removes or narrows the real shared findings exposed by the first scan. Reusing artifacts across the two independent existing workflows was rejected because correlating two asynchronously completed runs to one exact PR head adds race and stale-artifact risk; `--retain-public` was rejected because it would hide unused shared public declarations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Maintainers now get a zero-findings dead-code gate for shared Swift code without false positives from APIs used by only one native app.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Local Periphery 3.7.4 prototype: initial consumer reports intersected at 455 Swift USRs; 382 were generated protocol declarations and 73 were hand-written shared declarations.\n- Final clean consumer scans: iOS 107 platform-local findings, macOS 202 platform-local findings, shared intersection 0.\n- `node scripts/periphery-intersection.mjs ...`: zero shared findings.\n- `corepack pnpm test test/scripts/periphery-intersection.test.ts test/scripts/test-projects.test.ts`: 201 passed.\n- `corepack pnpm check:changed`: passed on Blacksmith Testbox (`tbx_01kxcbr0gyy27m5y5gp4qcczsa`, [Actions run 29214080240](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29214080240)).\n- `swift test --no-parallel`: all touched suites pass; the full local package run reaches 741/742 and stops on the unrelated existing `WatchCommandsTests` unknown-payload fixture.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n",
